From f8d8dd4fec7ce947f97c4447038a64c5ff5eaf60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ultras <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:08:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] hw/arm: add MediaTek MT7981B router machine
 (mt7981-router)

A configurable MT7981B (Filogic 820) router board that boots unmodified
firmware through the real boot chain: emulated BootROM -> BL2 (DRAM
training) -> BL31 + U-Boot (FIP) -> OpenWrt from SPI-NAND.

SoC: 2x Cortex-A53, GICv3, UARTs, TOPRGU watchdog, APXGPT timers,
DRAMC with responses that let MediaTek's binary DRAM calibration find
real windows (DDR3/DDR4), SPIM + SPI-NAND (W25N01GV/W25N02KV, folder
of partition dumps as backing store), frame engine (QDMA/PDMA, TSO,
checksum offload), LynxI SGMII PCS, GPIO/EINT, xHCI + IPPC, WED reset
bits, Wi-Fi (WFDMA + emulated WM/WA firmware interface, radio silent),
thermal sensor, TRNG, EIP-97 ID.

Board options: gmac0 = mt7531 switch (with port labels) | rtl8221b |
yt8821 | none, gmac1 = rtl8221b | yt8821 | gphy (built-in PHY) | none,
nand = 128 | 256, ddr = ddr3 | ddr4 (checked against the preloader),
usb-port = none | 2 | 3, PHY reset / button GPIOs, reset-hold for
U-Boot TFTP recovery.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
